# What ends up in the Composer package.
#
# `export-ignore` removes a path from `git archive`, which is what Packagist
# builds the dist archive from — so it is what `composer require` downloads by
# default. It does not touch the repository: the files below stay in git, stay
# on GitHub, and `composer install --prefer-source` still clones all of them.
# In particular the demo gif keeps rendering in the README on GitHub, because
# that page is served from the repository and not from the archive.
#
# The point is weight, and the weight is one file. The whole tree is 4.7 MB,
# `src/` is 619 KB of it, and `docs/demo.gif` alone is 3.4 MB. A library whose
# selling point is that it runs on shared hosting should not make every install
# pay for a screen recording.
#
# `demo/` is deliberately **not** excluded. It costs 54 KB — less than a tenth
# of `src/` — and it is self-contained: `seed.php` generates its own catalogue
# and the only thing it reaches for is `../src/autoload.php`, which is in the
# archive. Two commands from inside `vendor/ols/php-fts` and there is a working
# search page to click on, which is worth a great deal more than 54 KB.
#
# Kept: src/, demo/, composer.json, LICENSE, and the three markdown files a
# reader might want from inside vendor/.

/tests/         export-ignore
/docs/          export-ignore
/benchmark/     export-ignore
/tools/         export-ignore
/.github/       export-ignore

/phpunit.xml    export-ignore
/phpstan.neon   export-ignore
/.gitignore     export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
